# Sync
1. Set playlists in `playlists.json`
2. Run `python sync.py`

sync only playlists with this name:
`python sync.py --playlist "Techno"`

# troubleshooting
large playlists will hit rate limits.

# Setup
Steps:
1. Find your SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID and SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET

Go to the Spotify Developer Dashboard and log in with the same Spotify account you want the playlists synced into. Spotify currently requires Premium for Web API use.

https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api?query=uri&utm_source=chatgpt.com

Redirect URI: https://127.0.0.1:8888/callback

2. Set the Client ID and Secret

in .env set
```
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here`
```

3. Generate your SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN

`python get_refresh_token.py`

The page itself will probably fail to load or show a security warning. That's expected for this script. It doesn't have a local HTTPS server listening there; it just wants Spotify to put the temporary authorization code into the URL.

Copy the entire URL from your browser address bar.

4. Add the refresh token to .env
SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN=your_actual_refresh_token`